"""Unified asynchronous workout analysis: Stages A -> B -> C -> D.

    A  V-JEPA 2.1      sample the file, embed every window, classify, find reps
    B  latent dynamics trajectory consistency -> the 1-3 worst moments
    C  SAM 2.1         segment those moments into candidate regions
    D  Gemini          look at the video and those keyframes, write the report

Stages A-C are local and produce MEASUREMENTS. Stage D is remote and produces
JUDGEMENT. Keeping that line visible is the point of the split: every number the
report leans on exists in the response independently of what Gemini said about
it, so a claim can be checked rather than taken on trust.

VRAM DISCIPLINE (4 GB RTX 3050)
    Two vision backbones never sit in VRAM together. V-JEPA belongs to the
    caller and stays loaded; SAM is pulled in for Stage C and released before
    Stage D starts. `torch.cuda.empty_cache()` runs at every handoff. The whole
    pipeline is serialised by the caller -- two concurrent uploads on this card
    is an OOM, not a feature.
"""

import gc
import json
import time
from pathlib import Path

import numpy as np
import torch

import config
import voice
